# Cr2 -- the Q1 target case for FCIQMC (docs/FCIQMC_RESEARCH_SCOPE.md).
#
# NOT a regression case. Two atoms, and the active space is what blocks it:
#
#   CAS(12,12)  853,776 dets      ~1.3 h   reachable today
#   CAS(12,14)    9.0M dets       ~2 d     painful
#   CAS(12,16)   64.1M dets       ~47 d    out of reach
#   CAS(12,18)  344.6M dets       ~2 yr    out of reach, AND 2.76 GB per CI
#                                          vector (~22 GB for a Davidson subspace)
#
# The 12 active electrons are the 3d^5 4s^1 valence on each Cr. The sextuple
# Cr-Cr bond is the textbook hard multireference case -- single-reference methods
# get the binding curve qualitatively wrong -- so the larger active spaces are
# chemically motivated, not invented to be big.
#
# As committed this runs CAS(12,12), which SHOULD complete: it is the reachable
# rung, and it exists so the boundary can be verified rather than asserted.
# Raise nactorb to 14/16/18 to walk off the cliff.

%begin_control
    basis       sto-3g
    calculation energy
    verbosity   normal
    basis_type  cartesian
%end_control

%begin_scf
    scf_type    rhf
    correlation casscf
    nactele     12
    nactorb     12
    ci_max_dim  1000000
    use_diis    .true.
    diis_dim    8
    save_checkpoint .false.
    engine      os
    guess       sad
%end_scf

%begin_geom
    coord_type  cartesian
    coord_units angstrom
    use_symm    .false.
%end_geom

%begin_coords
2
0   1
Cr    0.000000     0.000000     0.000000
Cr    0.000000     0.000000     1.680000
%end_coords
